+### Optimization applied (factories phase)
+
+1. **`spec/support/factory_optimization.rb`** (new, scoped helper):
+   ```ruby
+   module FactoryOptimization
+     def self.skip_side_effects?(transient_opt_in: nil, tag_opt_in: nil)
+       return false if transient_opt_in
+       return false unless defined?(RSpec) && RSpec.respond_to?(:current_example)
+       example = RSpec.current_example
+       return false if example.nil?
+       return false unless [:model, :request].include?(example.metadata[:type])
+       return false if tag_opt_in && example.metadata[tag_opt_in]
+       return false if example.metadata[:with_factory_side_effects]
+       true
+     end
+     def self.skip_bookmark?(transients) ... end
+     def self.skip_login_activities?(transients) ... end
+   end
+   ```
+   Loaded via `rails_helper` `spec/support/**/*.rb` before lazy `load_definitions`, available in callbacks (callbacks run during tests). Returns `false` (preserve old behavior) for other types, outside RSpec, or on error.
+
+2. **`spec/fabricators/status_fabricator.rb`** (scoped skip + fast URI):
+   - `transient :with_bookmark`
+   - `after_build`: `Faker::Internet.device_token` → `"https://example.com/statuses/#{Fabrication::Sequencer.sequence(:status_remote_uri)}"` (global seq, unique, no I18n).
+   - `after_create do |status, transients|`: `unless FactoryOptimization.skip_bookmark?(transients); Fabricate(:bookmark, status: status); end`
+
+3. **`spec/fabricators/user_fabricator.rb`** (scoped skip + fast email, inherits to `admin/moderator/owner/private_user`):
+   - `transient :with_login_activities`
+   - `email`: `"#{i}#{Faker::Internet.email}"` → `"user#{i}@example.com"`
+   - `after_create do |user, transients|`: `unless FactoryOptimization.skip_login_activities?(transients); 2.times { Fabricate(:login_activity, user: user) }; end`
+
+4. **Hot `Faker` → fast sequences (global, behavior-preserving, unique + valid)**:
+   - `account_fabricator`: `username`: `Faker::Internet.user_name...` → `"user#{i}"`
+   - `tag_fabricator`: `name`: `Faker::Lorem.word` → `"tag#{i}"`
+   - `domain_block`, `email_domain_block`, `unavailable_domain`, `preview_card_provider`, `instance_moderation_note`: `domain`: `"#{i}#{Faker::Internet.domain_name}"` → `"example#{i}.com"` (align with `domain_allow`)
+   - `canonical_email_block`, `email_subscription`: `email` → `"user#{i}@example.com"`
+   - `username_block`: `username`: `Faker::Internet.username` → `"blockeduser#{i}"`
+   - `login_activity`: `ip` → `'127.0.0.1'`, `user_agent` → `'TestAgent'` (no uniqueness needed)
+   - `tagged_object`: `uri`: `Faker::Internet.device_token` → `sequence(:tagged_object_uri) { "https://example.com/tagged/#{i}" }`
+   - Cold `Faker` (`Lorem` paragraphs, `preview_card`, `webhook`, `fasp`, `terms` dates) left unchanged (negligible, minimize risk).
+
+### Why this is safe
+
+- Bookmarks: no `Bookmark.count` assertions; `cleanup_policy` self-checks use different account (verified `self_status_reference_exists` SQL); `export`/`bookmarks`/`backup`/`bulk_import` use explicit `Fabricate(:bookmark, account: X)` + `contain_exactly` (auto by other account doesn't pollute). Verified with `verify_factory_opt_spec` (model/request skip, service preserve, transient/tag opt-ins).
+- LoginActivities: only relative `change.by(1)` in `omniauth` (filtered 0 ex without OIDC) + `sessions_controller` `change(user.login_activities.where(success: true),:count).by(1)` (type `:controller`, preserves old behavior, still passes). No absolute counts. `login_activity_spec` uses `build`.
+- Faker: uniqueness via sequences (per-model namespace `account_username`, `user_email`, etc., global increment, no rollback collisions); validity checked against `USERNAME_RE`, `HASHTAG_NAME_RE`, `DomainValidator`, email format; explicit values in specs that assert (`tag: 'foo'`, `domain: 'example.com'`, `username: 'alice'`) unaffected. Other types (services/controllers/lib) get fast values too but still pass (verified `backup_service` 2.26s, `feed_manager` 9.11s, `sessions_controller` 2.42s, all 0 failures).
+- Other types preserve side effects (scoped check), so `services`/`controllers`/`lib`/`system` behavior unchanged except faster Faker strings. `rails runner` (no `RSpec.current_example`) preserves old behavior.
+- `status.uri` for local stays `nil` (filled by `store_uri`); remote uses `https://example.com/statuses/N` unique via `Sequencer` (no collision with explicit `https://already.bookmarked/1` etc.).
+- No app code changes, no assertion changes. Only factory + new support helper. Previous tags (`sidekiq_inline`, `enable_logging`, `need_notification_email`) untouched.
+
