+### Tags for future runs (factories + previous)
+
+- `with_bookmark: true` — (new, models/requests) opt into auto-`Bookmark` for `Fabricate(:status)`. Or transient `Fabricate(:status, with_bookmark: true)`. No current spec needs it (all create bookmarks explicitly when needed).
+- `with_login_activities: true` — (new, models/requests) opt into 2x `LoginActivity` for `Fabricate(:user)`/`admin_user`/`moderator_user`/`owner_user`. Or transient `Fabricate(:user, with_login_activities: true)`. No current spec needs it (only relative deltas asserted).
+- `with_factory_side_effects: true` — (new, generic) opt into both side effects for models/requests. Use if a future spec asserts on auto-created records.
+- Previous: `sidekiq_inline: true` (3 model email specs), `enable_logging: true` (none), `need_notification_email: true` (requests, none) — still valid, untouched.
+- Future ideas (not applied): `Paperclip post_process` stub for non-media models/requests with `media_processing: true` opt-out (~2-4% models, ~7% in `cleanup_policy` profile, but needs audit of `blurhash`/`thumbnail` assertions); `Lorem` → static text (<1%); `web_push` EC key memoization (<0.1s); `Faker::Date.unique` in `terms` (9 refs) → static date. Combined models+requests already over 2x, so further factory work is diminishing returns — next bottleneck is `MediaAttachment` (6.72s, real ffmpeg) and `PG exec` (10% self) + `GC marking` (12.9% self, reduced indirectly by fewer records).
